logy  in general is likely to continue  still musk plans to continue upgrading  tesla's advanced driver resistance  technology the car is kind of a robot on  four wheels and and so then well you  know  we could probably take that same  technology and and put it in a humanoid  robot and have that rogue be useful that  next iteration could be the teslabot  which musk unveiled in august it's a  humanoid robot that musk hopes will  perform generic robotic tasks for humans  man starship is a hard hard hard hard  project this is the the biggest rocket  ever made  this year musk also continued to work on  starship which he aims to be the first  fully reusable orbital rocket this is  the rocket that he hopes will take  humans to the moon and mars so we made  the i think the most progressive  reusability that has been done but with  starship we're hoping to make the whole  thing reusable this is uh this is  profound like i said it's different it  is the difference between humanity being  a single planet species and a  multi-planet species it's it's really  that big of a deal in march musk  announced his plan to create a new city  in texas called starbase which he  envisions as the launch site for  starship and in may spacex successfully  landed its starship test vehicle on the  fifth attempt starship heading back to  the land  outside of starship spacex continues to  pave new ground the company launched the  first all-civilian flight to orbit  and it took nasa astronauts to the  international space station for the  second time this year thanks guys and  from endurance it was a great ride  better than we imagined the company also  won an exclusive nasa contract to build  a new lunar lander  starlink is really designed to serve the  the least served starlink musk's  broadband internet service also picked  up pace this year  the bulk of spacex's launches this year  have been related to starlink to getting  those broadband satellites into orbit  this year starlink underwent beta  testing in remote areas of the u.s  check this out starlink in july the  company said it had launched around 1800  satellites and is serving around 140 000  users in over 20 countries just two  instructions point the terminal uh at  the sky and plug it in star link  and start ship sort of fit together  starship is meant to be this enormous  rocket and um you can fit a lot of  starlink  satellites like inside of it to deploy  on december 2nd spacex carried out its  27th mission this year launching nearly  50 starlink satellites into orbit  during his wall street journal interview  musk sidestepped questions about his  future at tesla saying his ceo title is  made up i i changed my title to to  techno king  um  and by the way this is a formal sec  filing it's i'm legally  whatever techno king i just did that as  kind of like a joke because just just to  show that these titles don't mean a lot  days after that interview musk tweeted  possibly in jest that he was thinking of  quitting his jobs title preference aside  musk says he plans to deliver electric  vehicles from two new factories one in  texas and another in germany his other  challenge next year will be launching  the first starship prototype to orbit if  we are successful with this which i i  think we will be but i don't know if  we'll be either in 2022 i hope so  this is a profound revolution in access  to orbit the company has been working to  obtain various licenses and is currently  waiting on an environmental review from  the faa which is expected by the end of  the year starlink also plans to obtain  permission from regulatory agencies to  launch even more satellites next year  spacex has asked the  sort of telecoms regulator in the u.s  for example for permission to  build out a what's called a  constellation sort of a network of of  satellites of about 30 000 of those  devices beyond 2022 musk says he's  excited to introduce the electric  vehicle pickup truck that tesla is  aiming to produce in volume in 2023.  gonna be an incredible product i think  it's it may be our our best product ever  and i think it probably will be between  electric vehicles and rockets the years  ahead may be even more demanding for  musk but could also lead to more banner  moments for the billionaire ceo

